change:
  id: CHG-005
  title: Local hybrid GraphRAG and evolutionary memory
  status: delivered
  intent: Experimentally compare no, semantic, structural and hybrid retrieval treatments while preserving deterministic fitness as the sole selection authority.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - SYS-001
    - ARCH-001
    - ARCH-002
    - ADR-0004
    - RISK-001
    - RISK-004
    - RISK-005

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: The mutation proposer receives an explicit bounded retrieval bundle selected before model invocation, while candidate validation, fitness and promotion semantics remain unchanged.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: HYBRID retrieval runs for a known production target whose implementation is semantically relevant and whose connected test or constraint is not among the closest vector matches
        then: the bundle contains both semantic implementation and structurally connected evidence, excludes unrelated evidence and fits the configured evidence/context budgets
        and:
          - every item has stable provenance, authority/status and selection reasons
          - the exact bundle reaches the mutation proposer
          - candidate provenance records retrieval mode, configuration and evidence ids
          - deterministic evaluation receives the same candidate/evidence types and remains authoritative
      - id: S2
        when: retrieval mode is NONE
        then: no Neo4j or embedding dependency is constructed and existing proposal/candidate semantics are preserved
        and:
          - the empty retrieval bundle is recorded with the NONE treatment
      - id: S3
        when: repository evidence is indexed twice at the same revision or a source is removed
        then: stable identities and content revisions are deterministic, repeated indexing is idempotent and stale repository projections are removed
        and:
          - Neo4j deletion remains recoverable by rebuilding from repository sources
      - id: S4
        when: GRAPH or HYBRID is configured and Neo4j is unavailable, unindexed or projected from a different repository revision
        then: the run fails clearly before model invocation and candidate creation
        and:
          - the run never silently changes treatment to NONE
          - stale projection diagnostics direct the operator to saaa-index update
      - id: S5
        when: an unchanged semantic document is indexed with the same embedding model
        then: its model-id/content-hash embedding is reused and a different content hash or model id invalidates the cache
        and:
          - embedding failure does not publish a partial graph revision
      - id: S6
        when: deterministic evaluation completes
        then: observable mutation, candidate, retrieved-evidence, changed-subject, check, benchmark, fitness and decision facts can be projected for bounded future retrieval
        and:
          - historical weighting is capped and visible
          - historical evidence cannot bypass a new deterministic evaluation
      - id: S7
        when: the same task corpus is run under NONE, VECTOR, GRAPH and HYBRID
        then: an ablation report compares accepted fitness improvement per mutation cost and acceptance per attempt with retrieval/token/cache diagnostics
        and:
          - the report makes no improvement claim without measured runs
      - id: S8
        when: deterministic evaluation completes and local SQLite state is later absent
        then: a compact Git-visible experiment envelope retains both subject and SAAA process revisions, strategy/configuration IDs and observable deterministic outcomes and can rehydrate the evolutionary-memory ledger used to rebuild the graph
        and:
          - prompts, raw model responses, embeddings and private reasoning are excluded
          - the generated wiki experiment page is visibly non-authoritative
      - id: S9
        when: accumulated experiment history exceeds the graph working-set policy
        then: the versioned lineage-novelty policy selects a bounded set using champions, known ancestry, failure fingerprints, novelty and a deterministic exploration reservoir rather than age
        and:
          - policy bounds are overrideable without silently changing the policy id
          - durable envelopes are not deleted and retained strategies gain no automatic fitness authority
      - id: S10
        when: an historic repository revision is explicitly re-inflated
        then: repository facts come from that commit and only outcome records compatible with that revision enter the bounded graph working set
        and:
          - JGit is the zero-setup primary API and native Git fallback is visible
          - the current checkout is not modified
      - id: S11
        when: a subject implementation is evolved by a versioned SAAA process
        then: one Neo4j database partitions both repository projections and links an explicit evolution context to subject, process and retrieval configuration identities
        and:
          - replacing one repository projection does not erase another
          - public command tokens use the saaa- namespace rather than generic tool names

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: deterministic/HybridRetrievalAcceptanceTest.suppliesSemanticAndStructurallyConnectedEvidenceWithinBudgetToTheProposer
    layer: component
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/HybridRetrievalAcceptanceTest.noneSuppliesAnEmptyBundleWithoutGraphAccess
    layer: component
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: adapters/RepositoryEvidenceIndexerTest.isIdempotentAndRemovesStaleProjectionFacts
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: adapters/Neo4jEvidenceGraphIntegrationTest.unavailableGraphFailsConfiguredRetrievalBeforeProposal
    layer: integration
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: adapters/SqliteRetrievalProjectionStoreIntegrationTest.reusesAndInvalidatesEmbeddingsByModelAndContentHash
    layer: integration
  - scenario: S6
    test_id: deterministic/EvolutionaryMemoryProjectorTest.projectsOnlyObservableOutcomeEvidenceWithBoundedHistoricalWeight
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S7
    test_id: deterministic/RetrievalAblationRunnerTest.comparesIdenticalTasksAcrossAllRetrievalModes
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S8
    test_id: adapters/GitExperimentEnvelopeStoreIntegrationTest.roundTripsReviewableEnvelopeAndGeneratesANonAuthoritativeWikiProjection
    layer: integration
  - scenario: S9
    test_id: deterministic/LineageNoveltyMemoryPolicyTest.selectsByEvolutionaryValueAndKeepsKnownChampionLineageWithinABound
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S10
    test_id: adapters/GitRepositoryRevisionIntegrationTest.createsAndCleansAnHistoricSnapshotWithoutChangingTheCheckout
    layer: integration
  - scenario: S11
    test_id: adapters/Neo4jEvidenceGraphIntegrationTest.replacesRepositoryProjectionAndTraversesAnExplicitStructuralRelationship
    layer: integration

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: record the intentional undefer decision, retrieval contracts, explicit proposer request seam, NONE behavior and provenance scaffolding
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: add on-demand Neo4j Community Compose, deterministic repository projection and bounded GRAPH retrieval
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: add versioned Evidence Capsule compilation and separate SQLite memoisation/provenance storage
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: add provider-neutral embeddings, LangChain4j adapter, embedding cache and Neo4j vector index for VECTOR
    status: completed
  - id: T5
    slice: add exact seeds, deterministic reciprocal-rank fusion, HYBRID budgets and complete proposer provenance
    status: completed
  - id: T6
    slice: project observable evaluation outcomes as bounded evolutionary memory
    status: completed
  - id: T7
    slice: add identical-corpus retrieval ablation metrics and structured reports
    status: completed
  - id: T8
    slice: document operation, measured results and the Neo4j justification decision after validation
    status: completed
  - id: T9
    slice: separate durable experiment memory from disposable retrieval caches and add Git envelopes plus a generated non-authoritative wiki projection
    status: completed
  - id: T10
    slice: add versioned evolutionary-value graph working-set policy and explicit historic reinflation
    status: completed
  - id: T11
    slice: relate subject and process repository revisions in one partitioned graph and namespace public command tokens
    status: completed
  - id: T12
    slice: prefer pinned JGit APIs for read-only repository operations with visible native Git fallback and security evidence
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - generic RAG platform or background indexing service
  - OpenSearch, Elasticsearch or another vector database
  - broad AST framework or LSP integration
  - distributed workers, Kubernetes or production deployment
  - LLM reranking
  - model-authored score, approval or promotion
  - automatic merge to main

risks:
  - RISK-004 stale or historically self-reinforcing evidence can contaminate retrieval experiments
  - RISK-005 current Neo4j images contain known Java findings; the selected digest is loopback-only and HTTP-disabled until an upstream patched image is available
  - Neo4j may add more operational cost than distinct structural evidence value
  - the live loop remains on transitional Mutation while MutationContract is not yet wired end to end
  - semantic retrieval quality cannot be claimed from deterministic fake embeddings used by tests
